  "id": "privileged-access",
  "term": "privileged access",
  "definition": "In this context, privileged access means that certain social signals, especially interactive gestures, enter and influence a person’s perceptual and motor systems more readily than other gestures. This stronger access appears as an automatic tendency to prepare a response, even when the gesture is not relevant to the task at hand.",
